          and an empty expected result (ck.db `zephyr_cases`).  No STEP heading below can
          therefore quote authored text.  The expected behaviour used to grade this case
          comes from the product's own documents, quoted here because the whole case
          turns on them.
            1. "X960 platform support TPS", row 271:
                 Management | Show warning message when user continue to use default PW
                 | Priority 1 | Supported: YES
            2. "Warning when using default password TFS", project 2616, revision 0.3,
               approved October 2021.  Spec 2616.1, verbatim:
                 "The system will check at every login using the default account
                  'manager' if the factory default password 'friend' is set, if it is,
                  the system will warn the user that the default password should be
                  changed."
               and its worked example, verbatim:
                 awplus login: manager
                 Password:
                 AlliedWare Plus (TM) 0.0.0 09/26/21 21:23:17
                 % Default password needs to be changed.
                 awplus>
               The same TFS says: new commands None, logging specifications None,
               licensing none, Initial Release Targets "all platforms in 5.5.1-2",
               Excluded Targets None.
            So the expected string is exactly `% Default password needs to be changed.`.
            It must appear after the version banner and just before the first prompt, at
            EVERY login as `manager` while the password is `friend`.  It needs no
            configuration and no licence.  The DUT runs a build far newer than 5.5.1-2.
            The TFS names no log line and no show command, so the login byte stream is
            the only place this can be graded.
          The eight steps below were designed by the tester from those documents.
